# Push new build (building-map-explorer)

When the user asks to push, deploy, publish, or go live:

## Remember

- **Live site builds from GitHub `main` source code**, not uncommitted local files.
- **Map data** lives in Supabase — edits while signed in take effect immediately (no JSON sync step).
- **Never commit** `.env.local` or files containing secrets.

## Standard push

1. `git pull origin main`
2. `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test`
3. `git status` — review changes; stage only intended files
4. `git commit -m "…"` with a clear message
5. `git push origin main` → triggers `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` (test + build + GitHub Pages)

Or use:

```powershell
npm run push-live
```

## After push to main

- Watch: https://github.com/quadreal-r/building-map-explorer/actions
- Live: https://quadreal-r.github.io/building-map-explorer/
- Hard-refresh when deploy finishes (~5–10 min)

## R2 media (when picture/document binaries changed)

```powershell
npm run upload-rtu-pictures-r2 -- --from-folder "C:/path/to/pictures"
npm run upload-rtu-documents-r2 -- --from-folder "C:/path/to/docs" --skip-existing
```

Picture/document **metadata** is in Supabase — update via the app while signed in, or run `npm run migrate-json-to-supabase` for bulk legacy import.

## User shortcut phrase

If they say **"Everything is good now, push the code"**: pull, test, commit, push to `main`, report Actions URL.

